-- title:
--   Ordinary H₁ local ring as W₀[[t]][X]/(g), g Eisenstein-like
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, naturals $\ell_g, M'$ with $\ell_g$ prime, $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$, $M' \neq 0$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$, and a commutative ring $A_0$. Assume the three equivariance statements over all $A_0$-algebras $T$: a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point datum $(x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q)$ (affine Weierstrass equation at $(x_P,y_P)$, $(\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{\ell_g})(x_P)=0$, $x_Q=x_P$, $y_Q=y_P$) transforms to one for $C\bullet W$; the $\Gamma_0(p^k)$ kernel condition `IsGamma0PowAt` is preserved under `kernelVariableChangeDeg`; and divisibility of `inLineMulPoly` is preserved likewise. Fix a family $\mathcal{G}$ of relative group laws on the projective models (chord-tangent, with origin as identity), a level transport $\mathcal{T}$ for Drinfeld $q$-bases satisfying the section-transport compatibilities, and an abstract representing package $P_0$, with ring $B_0$ and universal point, for the moduli datum of `rigidDataH1Pow`; let $x$ be a raw object over $B_0$ (curve of unit discriminant with $\Gamma_0(M')$ kernel polynomials, a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point, a Drinfeld $q$-basis pair, and the link divisibility) whose class is the universal point. Let $R$ be a Noetherian local ring, complete for its maximal ideal, an $A_0$-algebra, with $\iota : B_0 \to R$; let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$ in which $\ell_g$ and $M'$ are nonzero, $\mathrm{res}_R : R \twoheadrightarrow k$ with kernel the maximal ideal; let $W_0$ be a complete discrete valuation domain with maximal ideal $(q)$ and residue map $\mathrm{res}_0$ onto $k$, with $R$ a $W_0$-algebra compatibly with $A_0$ and residues. Assume the factorisation property: for every Artinian local $W_0$- and $A_0$-algebra $T$ with residue map to $k$ compatible with $\mathrm{res}_0$, every $A_0$-algebra map $B_0 \to T$ lifting $\mathrm{res}_R \circ \iota$ extends uniquely to a residue-compatible $W_0$-algebra map $R \to T$. Finally let $F_0$ be a formal group over $k$ whose power series is the fixed formal group law of the reduction along $\mathrm{res}_R$ of the curve of the Drinfeld component of $\iota_* x$, and assume $[q]_{F_0} = u X^q$ with $u$ a unit. Then there is a monic $g \in W_0[[t]][X]$ of degree $q-1$ whose coefficients in degrees $< q-1$ lie in the maximal ideal of $W_0[[t]]$, with constant coefficient $q$ times a unit, and $R$ is isomorphic to $W_0[[t]][X]/(g)$ as a $W_0$-algebra.
--
--   This is the Igusa-type local presentation of the completed local ring of the fine moduli problem with $\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ structure and full Drinfeld $q$-level structure, at a point where the reduced formal group is ordinary: the ring is a $W_0[[t]]$-algebra generated by a root of an Eisenstein-like monic polynomial of degree $q-1$. It feeds the integrality and reducedness statements about such completed local rings used in the study of the relevant modular curves and their Hecke algebras.
